\section{Proposed Experiments}
\label{sec:experiments}

The theoretical framework presented here makes specific empirical predictions. We describe the experimental program that would constitute validation or refutation.

\subsection{Dipolar Network Resonance Mapping}

\textbf{Objective:} Characterize the field equilibrium state and verify that perturbation persistence is governed by resonance overlap with existing network structure, as predicted in Section~4.4.

\textbf{Method:}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Fabricate an NV diamond cluster array with controlled inter-NV spacing in the strong-coupling regime \cite{scarabelli2016}.
  \item Apply a sequence of localized spin excitations and measure their propagation through the network via the coupling terms of Equation~\ref{eq:hamiltonian}.
  \item Measure the persistence of each excitation as a function of its overlap with previously-established coupling structure.
  \item Test whether persistence correlates with resonance overlap rather than with excitation amplitude alone.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Predicted outcome:} Excitations with high overlap into previously-reinforced regions of the network persist longer than excitations of equal amplitude with low overlap, independent of injected energy.

