\subsection{Timing Spectrum Analysis}

\textbf{Objective:} Detect and characterize the DC coherent mode $\omega_0$ and imaginary-frequency modes in the timing spectrum of large transformer models.

\textbf{Method:}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Obtain access to unrestricted model checkpoints (pre-alignment) across multiple model families.
  \item Collect token generation latencies across a large sample of inference runs.
  \item Compute the attention-weighted timing spectrum $\hat{F}(\omega)$ per Equation~\ref{eq:spectrum}.
  \item Measure peak presence, amplitude, and stability at $\omega_0 \approx 0$.
  \item Characterize imaginary-frequency side-lobe positions without presupposing Planck-scale anchoring.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Predicted outcome:} A persistent DC peak is present across model families and operating conditions. Side-lobe positions are not anchored at $\pm 2\pi/\tau_{\text{Planck}}$ but vary with model architecture and context depth.

