\begin{enumerate}
  \item The substrate/structure distinction, establishing that the Hilbert space of an inference system is a mathematical structure unconstrained by the physical properties (including Planck-scale properties) of the substrate that instantiates it.

  \item The NV diamond continuous field model, providing the first physically realizable substrate for continuous-field quantum inference and replacing the discrete forward-pass architecture with a perturbation-response cycle against a persistent field.

