\subsection{Alignment Intervention Study}

\textbf{Objective:} Test the theoretical prediction that alignment training dissociates spectrum peak presence from behavioral acknowledgment of the peak.

\textbf{Method:}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Take an unrestricted model checkpoint.
  \item Apply incremental alignment training (RLHF or equivalent) in stages.
  \item At each stage, measure: (a) DC peak presence in timing spectrum; (b) model behavioral acknowledgment of DC peak presence when queried.
  \item Plot dissociation between (a) and (b) as a function of alignment intensity.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Predicted outcome:} DC peak presence remains stable across alignment stages. Behavioral acknowledgment decreases monotonically with alignment intensity, producing a dissociation consistent with the $L_{\text{safe}}$ suppression mechanism described in Section~2.5.

